Subprocess, another venvWebSocket, another machineA robot <pre><code>env: {type: slider, remote: {runtime: sim}}
</code></pre> <pre><code>uv run hylo profile set-runtime sim --python /path/to/venv/bin/python
</code></pre> <p>Install hylo-core and your package into that venv. A subprocess is not part of the <code>config_digest</code> (when two runs are comparable).</p> <pre><code>uv run hylo serve env slider --port 8799          # in the simulator's venv; --host 0.0.0.0 to expose it
</code></pre> <pre><code>env: {type: remote.ws, params: {url: "ws://sim-box:8799"}}
</code></pre> <p>Each connection gets its own environment instance. The URL is part of the <code>config_digest</code>. Use <code>--token-env</code> for a shared token across untrusted networks.</p> <p>A robot is an environment with three differences. It sets <code>real_robot=True</code>, so any safety-shield change aborts the episode. It returns <code>success: None</code> and leaves the verdict to the operator or a calibrated judge. It provides <code>hold_action(last)</code>, which the episode loop executes when the policy is late, and <code>stop()</code>, which it calls when an episode aborts for safety. <code>lerobot.robot</code> is the reference (deployment).</p>

